[Music]  as fans of chicago fire now know jesse  spencer has left the building firehouse  51 that is in the fourth episode of the  show's 10th season his character matthew  casey goes to oregon to find out that  andy darden's sons aren't doing too well  after that he has a heart-to-heart  conversation with christopher herman in  which he basically says he is going to  leave chicago to help take care of them  in a subsequent episode casey deals with  the fallout from that decision including  his burgeoning romance with brett before  saying a final goodbye to the crew  spencer is one of the original chicago  firecast members having logged 200  episodes of the show since it started  airing in 2012. while his character is  supposedly going away for three years  there are no guarantees that the actor  will be back at all after such a long  time on the series though fans may be  wondering why the actor has decided to  leave now with the cat out of the bag  and his exit secured spencer has  explained his reasoning to the media in  a recent video interview with us weekly  spencer said that he actually wanted to  leave the show between its 9th and 10th  seasons but creator derek has talked him  into staying a few more episodes so he'd  have 200 of them on his resume as it  turned out his reasons for leaving the  show were entirely personal notably  spencer has been in network television  for 18 years straight which is obviously  a long time whichever way you cut it  spencer said there's other things that i  would like to do in the future and  there's some family that i need to take  care of  he added that he felt like his departure  storyline worked for him saying casey's  leaving and going to oregon therefore  for the right reasons you know it all  felt really organic but will spencer  return to the show at some point it's  possible in fact it sounds like talks  have already begun to bring him back to  tie up some loose ends during the same  interview haz was asked to spencer might  come back for a special occasion and he  gave an answer that should have fans  cautiously optimistic saying i'm hoping  i never try to predict what's going to  happen production-wise but we're in the  camp of whenever jesse wants to come do  an episode with us we will move  mountains on earth to make that happen  spencer clarified that he plans to stay  in chicago with his wife even though  he's stepping away from the show which  is a little ironic because the city's  harsh climate had him questioning  whether to remain on the series during  its early years obviously 200 episodes  on one tv show is a monumental  achievement for any actor and something  few in the profession will ever actually  experience it's also something that  spencer himself thought might not happen  in the early days of chicago fire cast  members leave shows or get let go for  any number of reasons ranging from  issues in their personal life to  decisions made by the writers for  spencer though it was the notoriously  frigid chicago winters that had him  unsure about his future on the series  during an interview with stage right  secrets about the 200th episode of  chicago fire spencer hailed the show's  crew as integral to the series longevity  while discussing the hard work the crew  regularly performed on the series he  made special mention of chicago's cold  temperatures spencer said i mean the  weather i didn't think i'd last a year  on the show after those winters i was  like i don't know if i can do this even  though he plans to stay in chicago now  that he has turned in his badge spencer  did indicate that he might start booking  vacations for himself during the winter  during his us weekly interview he said i  still am in chicago right now i'm not  running off to los angeles although i  might escape for a little bit of the  winter i might snowbird that's what i  hear people do wherever he goes here's  hoping he doesn't stray too far from the  windy city or the set of chicago 